rts  first there is the reason why you care  about dei  uh and so you you talk about what are  the things that are meaningful to you  about  improving representation or more  belonging  or those things and you'll just briefly  touch on that  theme and the theme will set up for the  second part which is a story that helps  illustrate why you care about that  aspect of  diversity equity and inclusion it should  be something real something that  happened it can be  something that relates to a business  situation that you've encountered where  you saw  an optimal result achieved because of  dei  or the opposite if the lack of  representation  didn't result in the outcome that you  were hoping for  so there's that story and you know if  there isn't a story that you feel  comfortable sharing about yourself  perhaps it's something that you've  noticed in another situation  that didn't directly happen to you that  made you think about why dei is  important  certainly the the events pertaining to  george floyd has caused many to to not  just hear about but also see  some of the reasons why this work  is important and impactful and so you  can talk about that  in your narrative and share maybe a  moment from your life  where it really hit home for you and  then  the last thing that i'll talk about in  the framework is a call to action so  you'll have the purpose yd matters to  you you'll have the story that connects  to that purpose and then lastly  some call to action and the call to  action is super important  in the call to action you want to make  sure that you're inviting people  to join you in the work because  hopefully  in parts one and two you've inspired  people to to understand  why they too should care about dei  and if they're ready to act you can  provide them a way to join you in the  work  the last thing that the sharia narrative  community does  is provide sort of a safe environment  for people to share  their narrative and to feel supported  and so they  man