 thousands of people all around the  world have heard  my story and narrative have been  encouraged by my journey as i've given  of myself  to talk about how it is that i came to  be in this space  and how i encourage other people to do  the same and so  there is this multiplicative effect of  each and every single one of those  individuals some of whom are engineers  like myself others are executives some  are in sales they come from all  different parts of google and all around  the world and they participate in this  community and also share their own  narratives  in places that we may not be able to see  and so there's a great  positive benefit of being able to see  these narratives grow and be shared  widely you know this really is about  scalability  right there's only so much that i can do  as an individual  but i want to make sure that i can  empower the next generation to do what  i'm doing and to do it even better  so that we can encourage more  inclusiveness and belonging in the space  now i just want to end with a couple of  final thoughts that i think are  important  first of all understand that knowledge  isn't power  not knowledge by itself knowledge  rightly applied  is powerful and that's really what this  is about a lot of us have been learning  over the past few months about why  the conversations about race about  inclusion  about belonging not just in tech but in  the world  why these things matter it's not enough  just to sit on that knowledge and not do  anything  it's important to do something and  sharing your narrative can be one of the  easiest ways  for you to be impactful in terms of  inviting other people to the  conversation inviting other people to  the work  now even though it's one of the easiest  ways it's still not  easy and i know that it takes you  sharing a bit of yourself that maybe you  didn't plan on sharing it work  and that's okay you're not alone  and one of the best things about the  share of your narrative program is that  it has  shown people that they're not alone i'm  not alone  as a person who has struggled through a  rough upbringing to become a software  engineer beating the odds  there are other people like me across  all different backgrounds and all  different shades  and that's really what belong is all all  about at the end of the day i know  that as a result of this program and  other things that i belong just as much  as anyone else because i'm a googler  and so i hope that this time has been  encouraging to you thank you for tuning  in to watch this presentation  and the best of luck to you and as you  pursue  greater diversity equity and inclusion  in your company or organization  thank you
 

